% ADJ52 case-13 program (this patient's observations + queries only; no rules).
% 53yo man, ~2 months progressive bilateral leg swelling (worse left), heaviness +
% easy leg tiring; marked pitting lower-limb oedema. Vigorous LV (EF ~70%, FS ~40%,
% SV ~85 mL, CO ~11 L/min). Modest pericardial fluid. Diuretic gave minimal relief.
% Intermittent mild chest tightness NOT clearly exertional. CT coronary angiography:
% tight diagonal-LAD stenosis (+ small effusion + pericardial thickening, not
% emphasized). Full anti-ischaemic therapy (antiplatelet + statin + beta-blocker) =
% no meaningful benefit. Then cough/sputum/worsening breathlessness + recurrent
% bilateral pleural effusions; thoracentesis of several litres relieved symptoms
% transiently but fluid promptly re-accumulated. Pleural fluid non-specific, LOW LDH
% (~105-110 U/L) and LOW ADA (~4 U/L). Mild anaemia, mildly low albumin, modest
% proteinuria. Dilated IVC (~24 mm), enlarged right chambers. Mitral inflow E
% respiratory variation >25%. No clear septal bounce; no Kussmaul sign. Re-review of
% earlier high-resolution CT: thickened pericardium >4.5 mm, previously obscured by
% effusion. Net: refractory reaccumulating right-sided fluid overload, normal EF,
% incidental coronary lesion, thickened pericardium with effusion.

% --- the unifying right-sided venous-congestion gestalt (counted once per dx) ---
observe symptom(marked_pitting_oedema_lower_limbs)
observe symptom(recurrent_bilateral_pleural_effusions)
observe ivc_dilated(over_twenty_mm)
observe right_chambers_enlarged

% --- the constriction-vs-restriction discriminators ---
observe ejection_fraction(preserved_hyperdynamic)
observe pericardium_thickness(over_four_mm)
observe mitral_e_respiratory_variation(over_twenty_five_percent)
observe septal_bounce(not_clearly_seen)
observe kussmaul_sign(absent)

% --- effusion biochemistry (transudate; argues against TB) ---
observe pleural_fluid_ldh(low)
observe pleural_fluid_adenosine_deaminase(low)

% --- the high-output features ---
observe cardiac_output(markedly_elevated)
observe lab(mild_anaemia)

% --- the coronary red herring ---
observe cta_finding(tight_stenosis_diagonal_lad)
observe chest_tightness_exertion_relation(not_related)
observe coronary_treatment_response(no_benefit)

% NOT observed (open, decision-relevant): cath_interdependence(...) and
% post_drainage_filling(...) — the two confirmatory discriminators.

% --- queries: each candidate diagnosis + the recommended next steps ---
? diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
? diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
? diagnosis(restrictive_cardiomyopathy)
? diagnosis(tuberculous_pericarditis)
? diagnosis(high_output_heart_failure)
? diagnosis(coronary_artery_disease)
? next_step(invasive_haemodynamic_catheterisation)
? next_step(cardiac_mri_with_late_gadolinium)
